<section class="container mt-9">
<div class="row seo-block">
<div class="col-sm-12">
<h2 class="title text-center">
What is sURL - short link or link shortener
</h2>
<div class="text">
<p>The term &ldquo;sURL&rdquo; is artificial and comes from two words: short and URL (Uniform Resource Locator). An analogue of the abbreviation URL is also the slang word &lsquo;link&rsquo; or &ldquo;reference&rdquo; in Ukrainian. Together, they form the term surl, which means a short analogue of a long link. This concept formed the basis for the name of the link shortening service Surl.li. From this point of view, sURL is a term designed to give a short name to shortened online addresses, and on the other hand, it is the proper name of the link shortening site where you are located. Today, Surl.li aims to become a service where users can manage short URLs to the site through their personal account and shorten links in one click online on our site without registration or payment.&nbsp;</p><p>We make every effort to ensure that every link from our service that you see on the web, in your SMS messages, or in messengers guarantees the safety of your transition. We are working on a system that verifies every shortened link. This way, you can safely follow short links.&nbsp;</p><p>The service is regularly updated and expanded with new features, from link statistics to new customized rates, from mass link shortening to a convenient API service. In the future, we will be able to shorten links not only on our domains, but also on your own. Add your own, register new domains with us, and expand without limits. Brand your own links, &ldquo;trim&rdquo; long links, and create short analogues.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="col-sm-12">
<h2 class="title text-center">
A Short Link Will Come in Handy for many reasons
</h2>
<div class="text">
<p>A short link is a complete analogue of a long URL. This allows you to transfer addresses of any length, such as links to specific products in an online store, or use additional parameters such as UTM. A short link stores the entire long link along with the parameters and simply redirects the user to the final URL. This completely eliminates a number of problems:<br>- Long links will not be truncated by messengers;<br>- Shortened URLs look equally good in advertising posts and presentations;<br>- You can use shortened addresses to generate simpler QR codes, which store fewer elements and are easier to recognize;<br>- The shortened link is easy to remember because it contains only a few characters.
The special value of short links is revealed in printed sources and presentations. Just imagine, all you need to do is print a link consisting of a few characters or generate a QR code from it, and anyone who sees such a link can easily follow it from their smartphone. Links for PDF or Word files &mdash; the short URL service sURL can do it all.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><h2>Short URLs available to English-speaking users worldwide</h2><p>SURL is a global link shortener designed for English-speaking audiences everywhere. Whether you&rsquo;re in the United States, the United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, New Zealand, India or any other country, you can shorten, manage and share your links with a fully English interface. The service works 24/7 with no regional restrictions and is suited for marketers, developers and social media teams. Explore our features to organize campaigns, track performance and scale your workflows with ease.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<div class="container faqs-section mt-6">
<div class="row">
<div class="col-12">
<div class="row">
<div class="accordion col-12" id="faq_6" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
<div class="accordion-item">
<h3 class="faq-toggle collapsed question" id="question_6"
role="button" itemprop="name" data-toggle="collapse"
data-target="#answer_6" aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="answer_6">
How to shorten links online?
</h3>
<div id="answer_6" class="collapse"
aria-labelledby="question_6"
data-parent="#faq_6">
<div class="faq-body answer" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
<span itemprop="text"><p>After entering your long link, you are given its shortened counterpart (surl or short url). The shortener program stores the connections between the short link and your link to the site. Thus, the link, regardless of its location, will redirect the user to the final URL. At the same time, you will save all parameters, for example, UTM tags, referral tags, link to site filters.</p></span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="accordion col-12" id="faq_7" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
<div class="accordion-item">
<h3 class="faq-toggle collapsed question" id="question_7"
role="button" itemprop="name" data-toggle="collapse"
data-target="#answer_7" aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="answer_7">
What do shortened link statistics show?
</h3>
<div id="answer_7" class="collapse"
aria-labelledby="question_7"
data-parent="#faq_7">
<div class="faq-body answer" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
<span itemprop="text"><p>Each shortened link has its own statistics, you can view them simply by adding a &quot;+&quot; sign to the short URL link, for example, surl.li/xxx+ In the link statistics you can see the number of clicks on the short link, the source of the transition and the geolocation of such transitions. Thus, our shortener becomes an indispensable tool for monitoring traffic to shortened addresses.</p></span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="accordion col-12" id="faq_8" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
<div class="accordion-item">
<h3 class="faq-toggle collapsed question" id="question_8"
role="button" itemprop="name" data-toggle="collapse"
data-target="#answer_8" aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="answer_8">
Is it safe to shorten a link online?
</h3>
<div id="answer_8" class="collapse"
aria-labelledby="question_8"
data-parent="#faq_8">
<div class="faq-body answer" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
<span itemprop="text"><p>Any link on the network can become public, remember this when generating shortened links to private or personal content. The process of shortening the address itself does not pose a threat to your security. It is important to remember about security measures when you follow third-party links unknown to you. It is also worth trusting only proven link shortening sites. We are working hard on the security of shortened links, and we conduct regular checks of final links. Also, users can <a data-fpl-component="primitive" href="https://surl.li/uk/check-short-url" rel="noopener" target="_blank">check short links</a></p></span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="accordion col-12" id="faq_9" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
<div class="accordion-item">
<h3 class="faq-toggle collapsed question" id="question_9"
role="button" itemprop="name" data-toggle="collapse"
data-target="#answer_9" aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="answer_9">
Need to reduce links in large quantities?
</h3>
<div id="answer_9" class="collapse"
aria-labelledby="question_9"
data-parent="#faq_9">
<div class="faq-body answer" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
<span itemprop="text"><p>If you need to shorten a large number of short links, use our <a data-fpl-component="primitive" href="https://dev.surl.li/v1" rel="noopener" target="_blank">API</a> , or the basic functionality available at <a data-fpl-component="primitive" href="https://surl.li/uk/bulk-shortening" rel="noopener" target="_blank">the link</a> .<br> Shorten hundreds of links with us and get thousands of clicks with statistics from Surli</p></span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="accordion col-12" id="faq_10" itemscope itemprop="mainEntity"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
<div class="accordion-item">
<h3 class="faq-toggle collapsed question" id="question_10"
role="button" itemprop="name" data-toggle="collapse"
data-target="#answer_10" aria-expanded="false"
aria-controls="answer_10">
Is this service an analogue of Google&amp;#39;s shortener?
</h3>
<div id="answer_10" class="collapse"
aria-labelledby="question_10"
data-parent="#faq_10">
<div class="faq-body answer" itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer"
itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
<span itemprop="text"><p>The once-famous goo.gl service was super popular, and the discontinuation of its support prompted the development of similar shorteners. clck, cuttly, bittly, and many others provide online link shortening. Some have ceased to exist, and we at Surl.li plan to develop the service and make it deeper and more convenient for managing your addresses.</p></span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
